<section class="chapter" id="c-line" data-side="l">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">01 / FABRIC PATH</span><span class="r">14 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>The web turns vertical to be sprayed</h2>
      <div class="es">Part129 · web 2 000 mm wide · 4.2 m path</div>
      <p>Fabric enters low, wraps a roller and climbs vertically through the gap between the two nozzle banks — which is why both faces can be treated in a single pass. It leaves over the top roller and drops away to the stenter chain.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Working width</span><b><em>2 400 mm</em></b></li>
        <li><span>Vertical pass</span><b>≈ 820 mm</b></li>
        <li><span>Faces treated</span><b>Both Sides</b></li>
        <li><span>Path length</span><b>4.23 m</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="c-frame" data-side="r">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">02 / BASE FRAME</span><span class="r">18 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>It bolts onto the stenter you already own</h2>
      <div class="es">miniheight2600 · DTFS bottom base m2026</div>
      <p>The unit is a retrofit. The base carries the tank, pump and dosing circuit at floor level and takes the spray duct on the frame above, so the whole assembly drops into the entry of an existing 2450 stenter without moving the machine.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Fits</span><b><em>Any Size</em></b></li>
        <li><span>Overall footprint</span><b>3.75 × 5.23 m</b></li>
        <li><span>Height class</span><b>2 600 mm</b></li>
        <li><span>Mounting</span><b>M16, bolted</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

