  <section class="chapter" id="c-pump" data-side="r">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">04 / PUMP &amp; STRAINER</span><span class="r">26 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>One pump, held at pressure</h2>
      <div class="es">1 HP pressure pump · 430 strainer ×2</div>
      <p>The nozzles are fed at constant pressure and the quantity is set by how long each one is held open, not by throttling the pump. That separation is what makes the add-on repeatable — pressure sets droplet size, duty cycle sets volume.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Pump</span><b><em>2 HP</em></b></li>
       <li><span>Line pressure</span><b id="linePr">3 bar</b></li> 
        <li><span>Line pressure</span><b>3 bar</b></li>
        <li><span>Strainers</span><b>2 × 430</b></li>
        <li><span>Feedback</span><b>Io Link Pressure Sensor</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="c-dose" data-side="l">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">05 / DOSING CIRCUIT</span><span class="r">30 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>Recipe changes happen in the valve block</h2>
      <div class="es">Festo DAPS-0015-090 ×16 · VZBA-½"-GGG-63</div>
      <p>Quarter-turn pneumatic actuators on stainless ball valves route liquor, water and air. Every route the operator would otherwise open by hand is automated here, so a recipe change is a command rather than a walk around the machine.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Actuators</span><b><em>16 × DAPS</em></b></li>
        <li><span>Ball valves</span><b>Festo VZBA, SS</b></li>
        <li><span>Pressure sensor</span><b>GP-M100/250/400</b></li>
        <li><span>Connections</span><b>½" &amp; 1" BSP</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="c-elec" data-side="r">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">06 / CONTROL</span><span class="r">34 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>Add-on follows line speed automatically</h2>
      <div class="es">Electrical control box · 1 200 × 1 100 mm</div>
      <p>The controller reads stenter speed and modulates nozzle duty cycle to hold grams per square metre constant. Speed up, duty rises; slow down for a seam and it drops. The operator sets a number, not a valve position.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Set point</span><b><em>g/m² add-on</em></b></li>
        <li><span>Tracks</span><b>Line speed</b></li>
        <li><span>Method</span><b>PWM per bank</b></li>
        <li><span>Duty now</span><b id="dutyNow">— %</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section> -->

  <section class="chapter" id="c-duct" data-side="l">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="hd"><span class="n">03 / SPRAY DUCT</span><span class="r">40 m/min</span></div>
      <h2>The part that does the work</h2>
      <div class="es">Spray_duct_subassembly · 74 parts · 777 800 tri</div>
      <p>Everything from here on is the duct assembly, loaded as its own file so it can be shown at full detail without the rest of the machine in the way. Two mirrored banks face each other across the web on a common tilting frame.</p>
      <ul class="fx">
        <li><span>Parts</span><b><em>74</em></b></li>
        <li><span>Bank separation</span><b>667 mm</b></li>
        <li><span>Duct length</span><b>2 816 mm</b></li>
        <li><span>Symmetry</span><b>Mirrored pair</b></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

